// NEGATIVE TEST -- the shift COUNT is in range and the VALUE still has no
// answer (N3-09).
//
// 63 is a legal amount for an i64, so the count check that owns
// tests/reject/const_shift_out_of_range.pd never fires here, and `checked_shl`
// answers Some: it only checks the count. What comes out is i64::MIN, which is
// not `1` scaled by 2^63 -- the number overflowed on the way. Measured before
// the guard: this was accepted and printed -2147483648.
//
// The test is the ROUND TRIP -- a shift that fits is undone by shifting back --
// so refusal names the operands rather than the bound. `1 << 62` fits, is
// evaluated here and emitted for C to evaluate again, and is pinned in
// tests/03_const_items.pd.
const X: i64 = 1 << 63;

fn main() {
    print_int(X);
}
